    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jung Hoo Lee** leads the charge with a 68.02 efficiency score, our strongest play of the day. Facing a favorable 5.16 xERA from Jose Cabrera, **Jung Hoo Lee** benefits from a projected #3 spot in the order and a +5% boost from wind-out conditions, making him our primary engine for AVG and run production. **Dylan Beavers** also profiles as an elite start at 63.47; he is attacking a soft matchup against Graceffo (5.08 xERA), and his ability to leverage a +7% platoon edge makes him a high-floor selection for our outfield rotation. While **Daulton Varsho** (51.34) and **Yainer Diaz** (45.22) are squaring off against the formidable Cole (3.38 xERA), their ability to maintain efficiency despite the pitching mismatch speaks to their high-contact profiles, though both are restricted by the difficulty of the matchup.\n\nThe bench decisions for this rotation were dictated by a combination of scheduling gaps and the scarcity of speed, as our primary run producers like **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Bryce Harper**, **Cal Raleigh**, and **Lawrence Butler** are all unavailable due to team off-days. With our core power bats resting, the optimizer leaned heavily toward the contact efficiency of **Jung Hoo Lee** and the speed-upside of **Dylan Beavers**. The final decision to start **Daulton Varsho** over potential bench depth came down to his dynamic platoon advantage against right-handed pitching, which slightly outclassed the internal projections for our remaining utility options. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given the caliber of the arms we are facing tonight. While **Jung Hoo Lee** carries a \"Lineup Pending\" tag, we are proceeding under the assumption he holds the #3 hole, though any shift down the order would trigger a re-evaluation of his current 68.02 score. We are keeping a close eye on **Yainer Diaz**, as his #7 spot in the order coupled with the elite arm of Cole represents the lowest ceiling in our active lineup today. We will continue to monitor the status of **Justin Crawford**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Will Smith**, **Matt Chapman**, **Luis Arraez**, **Masyn Winn**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **JJ Bleday**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Zack Gelof**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Braden Montgomery** to ensure our game caps remain optimized as we chase the league leaders in our 5x5 categories.",
